{"id": "section-body-00548", "title": "Triage Overview", "chapterId": "chapter-one", "blocks": [{"id": "body-00548", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading2", "text": "Triage Overview", "runs": [{"text": "Triage Overview"}], "level": 2, "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1890"}}, {"id": "body-00549", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Triage is the process of determining the priority of a patient to medical care based on the acuity (severity of condition) and capacity of the system to address the condition to optimize outcome.", "runs": [{"text": "Triage is the process of determining the priority of a patient to medical care based on the acuity (severity of condition) and capacity of the system to address the condition to optimize outcome."}]}, {"id": "body-00551", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Importance of Triage", "runs": [{"text": "Importance"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Triage"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-00553", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Triage enables quick identification of patients who need immediate attention and hence improves patient outcomes by avoiding potential delays. It helps in organizing, monitoring, evaluating and determining the department resources that patients might need.", "runs": [{"text": "Triage"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "enables"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "quick"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "identification"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patients"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "who"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "need"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "immediate"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "attention"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "hence"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "improves"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patient"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "outcomes"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "avoiding potential delays. It helps in organizing, monitoring, evaluating and determining the department resources that patients might "}, {"text": "need."}]}, {"id": "body-00555", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Triage system", "runs": [{"text": "Triage"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "system"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-00557", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "The triage system is based on recommendation of Emergency Medicine expert’s basic principles of triage, which uses specific criteria to categorize patients into three main levels of acuity:", "runs": [{"text": "The"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "triage"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "system"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "based"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "on"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "recommendation"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Emergency"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Medicine"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "expert’s"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "basic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "principles"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "triage,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "which"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "uses"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "specific criteria to categorize patients into three main levels of acuity:"}]}, {"id": "body-00559", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Emergency", "runs": [{"text": "Emergency"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-00561", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "All patients with immediate life or limb threats who are deemed salvageable, but likely to further decompensate without immediate intervention will be triaged in this level. This category can also be labeled as RED. Priority: those seriously injured/ill patients with potential to decompensate if not treated within 1 hour are triaged as priority cases. This category can also be labeled as YELLOW.", "runs": [{"text": "All patients with immediate life or limb threats who are deemed salvageable, but likely to further decompensate without immediate intervention will be triaged in this level. This category can also be labeled as 